1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
Matthew 21

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:08,820
Now when they drew near to Jerusalem and came to Bethphage, to the Mount of Olives,

3
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:11,860
then Jesus sent two disciples, saying to them,

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:18,000
Go into the village in front of you, and immediately you will find a donkey tied in a colt with her.

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,060
Untie them and bring them to me.

6
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:22,920
If anyone says anything to you, you shall say,

7
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:26,260
The Lord needs them, and he will send them at once.

8
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:30,700
This took place to fulfill what was spoken by the prophet, saying,

9
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:33,040
Say to the daughter of Zion,

10
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:38,300
Behold, your king is coming to you, humble and mounted on a donkey,

11
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,480
and on a colt, the foal of a beast of burden.

12
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:45,180
The disciples went and did as Jesus had directed them.

13
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:50,820
They brought the donkey and the colt and put on them their cloaks, and he sat on them.

14
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:54,500
Most of the crowd spread their cloaks on the road,

15
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:58,120
and others cut branches from the trees and spread them on the road.

16
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:02,480
And the crowds that went before him and that followed him were shouting,

17
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:05,900
Hosanna to the Son of David!

18
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:10,200
Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord!

19
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,640
Hosanna in the highest!

20
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:17,620
And when he entered Jerusalem, the whole city was stirred up, saying,

21
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:19,840
Who is this?

22
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:21,540
And the crowd said,

23
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:23,980
This is the prophet Jesus!

24
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,460
From Nazareth of Galilee!

25
00:01:27,340 --> 00:01:31,760
And Jesus entered the temple and drove out all who sold and bought in the temple,

26
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:36,620
and he overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those who sold pigeons.

27
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:37,900
He said to them,

28
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:39,640
It is written,

29
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:43,240
My house shall be called a house of prayer,

30
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:46,720
but you make it a den of robbers.

31
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:51,940
And the blind and the lame came to him in the temple, and he healed them.

32
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:54,480
But when the chief priests and the priests of the temple came,

33
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:57,500
and the scribes saw the wonderful things that he did,

34
00:01:57,880 --> 00:02:00,060
and the children crying out in the temple,

35
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:04,120
Hosanna to the Son of David!

36
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,740
They were indignant, and they said to him,

37
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:10,020
Do you hear what these are saying?

38
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:12,320
And Jesus said to them,

39
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:15,400
Yes, have you never read?

40
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:20,280
Out of the mouth of infants and nursing babies you have prepared praise.

41
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:24,280
And leaving them, he went out of the city to Bethany and Lodят,

42
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:31,440
there. In the morning, as he was returning to the city, he became hungry, and seeing a fig tree by

43
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:39,380
the wayside, he went to it and found nothing on it but only leaves. And he said to it, May no fruit

44
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:46,240
ever come from you again. And the fig tree withered at once. When the disciples saw it,

45
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:55,620
they marveled, saying, How did the fig tree wither at once? And Jesus answered them,

46
00:02:56,340 --> 00:03:02,980
Truly I say to you, if you have faith and do not doubt, you will not only do what has been done to

47
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:09,000
the fig tree, but even if you say to this mountain, Be taken up and thrown into the sea,

48
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:16,220
it will happen. And whatever you ask in prayer, you will receive, if you have faith.

49
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:23,940
And when he entered the temple, the chief priests and the elders of the people came up to him as he

50
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:29,060
was teaching, and said, By what authority are you doing these things? And who gave you this

51
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:37,220
authority? Jesus answered them, I also will ask you one question, and if you tell me the answer,

52
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:43,400
then I also will tell you by what authority I do these things. The baptism of John,

53
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:44,920
from where did it come?

54
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:46,220
From heaven.

55
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:51,320
From heaven or from man? And they discussed it among themselves, saying,

56
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:58,260
If we say from heaven, he will say to us, Why then did you not believe him? But if we say from man,

57
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:02,180
we are afraid of the crowd, for they all hold that John was a prophet.

58
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:09,460
So they answered Jesus, We do not know. And he said to them,

59
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:15,540
Neither will I tell you by what authority I do these things. What do you think?

60
00:04:15,540 --> 00:04:22,560
A man had two sons, and he went to the first and said, Son, go and work in the vineyard today.

61
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:29,960
And he answered, I will not. But afterward he changed his mind and went. And he went to the

62
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:37,840
other son and said the same. And he answered, I go, sir, but did not go. Which of the two

63
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:44,420
did the will of his father? They said, The first. Jesus said to them,

64
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:50,960
Truly I say to you, the tax collectors and the prostitutes go into the kingdom of God before you.

65
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:57,840
For John came to you in the way of righteousness, and you did not believe him. But the tax collectors

66
00:04:57,840 --> 00:05:03,740
and the prostitutes believed him. And even when you saw it, you did not afterward change your

67
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:07,780
minds and believe him. Hear another parable.

68
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:13,380
There was a master of a house, who planted a vineyard and put a fence around it and dug a

69
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:14,220
winepress in it. He put a vineyard and put a fence around it and dug a winepress in it,

70
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:18,940
and built a tower, and leased it to tenants and went into another country.

71
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:25,220
When the season for fruit drew near, he sent his servants to the tenants to get his fruit.

72
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:30,700
And the tenants took his servants and beat one, killed another, and stoned another.

73
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:36,060
Again he sent other servants more than the first, and they did the same to them.

74
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:43,700
Finally he sent his son to them, saying, They will respect my son. But when the tenants saw

75
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:44,400
the son, they did not believe him. And he said, I go, sir, but did not go. Which of the two did

76
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:49,300
they? They said to themselves, This is the heir. Come, let us kill him and have his

77
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:56,000
inheritance. And they took him and threw him out of the vineyard and killed him. When therefore

78
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:03,920
the owner of the vineyard comes, what will he do to those tenants? They said to him, He will put

79
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:09,820
those wretches to a miserable death, and let out the vineyard to other tenants, who will give him

80
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:13,540
the fruits in their seasons. Jesus said to them,

81
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:20,300
Have you never read in the Scriptures? The stone that the builders rejected has become the

82
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:28,640
cornerstone. This was the Lord's doing, and it is marvelous in our eyes. Therefore I tell you,

83
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:34,140
the kingdom of God will be taken away from you and given to a people producing its fruits.

84
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:41,000
And the one who falls on this stone will be broken to pieces. And when it falls on anyone,

85
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,820
it will crush him.

86
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:48,340
When the chief priests and the Pharisees heard his parables, they perceived that he was speaking

87
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:54,040
about them. And although they were seeking to arrest him, they feared the crowds because

88
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:55,800
they held him to be a prophet.

